# coverage-floors — per-package line-coverage floors, enforced by scripts/check.sh gate 6.
#
# A FLOOR IS A RATCHET. It is set from the MEASURED percentage of the first green build, not
# from an aspirational number, and it only ever goes UP. Guessing a floor produces one of two
# useless states: so low it gates nothing, or so high that the first honest commit is red and
# someone lowers it, which teaches everyone that the number is negotiable.
#
# A floor of 0 is COLLECT-ONLY: the package's coverage is measured and printed but not gated.
# That is the honest state for a package with no tests yet — visible, not absent. It is not a
# resting place; a package that gains tests gains a floor in the same PR.
#
# THE FILE IS A CLOSED WORLD. A package with measured statements and no record here fails the
# gate, because "new code arrived ungated" and "coverage held" must not emit the same green.
#
# Format:  package (module-relative) | floor (percent, integer)

internal/buildinfo | 100
cmd/<SERVICE>      | 0
